@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# FieldLog offline site map
+
+`natural-earth-50m.flg` contains worldwide Natural Earth 1:50 million coastline,
+lake outlines, and river and lake centerlines. The linework is generalized for
+regional views. Some viewports contain no mapped features. Keep the site marker
+and scale visible in those views.
+
+## Data provenance
+
+Natural Earth v5.1.2 Git revision `f1890d9f152c896d250a77557a5751a93d494776`
+supplies these inputs. The publisher places the data in the public domain and
+makes credit optional. “Made with Natural Earth” is the suggested credit.
+[Natural Earth terms of use](https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/)
+
+| Input | SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- |
+| [ne_50m_coastline.geojson](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/f1890d9f152c896d250a77557a5751a93d494776/geojson/ne_50m_coastline.geojson) | `271f1c4c1908312bac6b29d158ea1356544beafc129f260005300913aa5ea283` |
+| [ne_50m_lakes.geojson](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/f1890d9f152c896d250a77557a5751a93d494776/geojson/ne_50m_lakes.geojson) | `d350b75978b26fe839b797c2c529b2fb8f47fb3983c03f4964e36d5df9378a52` |
+| [ne_50m_rivers_lake_centerlines.geojson](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/f1890d9f152c896d250a77557a5751a93d494776/geojson/ne_50m_rivers_lake_centerlines.geojson) | `f286e0ce978fde999ca2d7a78c764be08542e19b63cded52b05c12d5173ccc51` |
+
+Keep the three filenames shown above and run
+`python3 -B Assets/SiteMap/encode-natural-earth.py INPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT`
+to reproduce the checked-in 860,633-byte asset. Its SHA-256 is
+`1c4a6e6add0fa4d3b7628a59d9bc2cde8782dad9fe4d135985fa153e12514379`.
+The encoder preserves path and ring boundaries, quantizes coordinates to signed
+E5 and normalizes +180° to −180°. The file has 2,789 paths and 105,835 vertices.
+
+## Native consumer contract
+
+Both `FieldLogModels` source directories contain matching copies of the model
+and scene types. Package the asset at an app-owned location, read at most
+`SiteMapGeography.maximumBytes`, and initialize `SiteMapGeography(data:)` once
+for the map owner. The asset has an `FLG1` header and a little-endian UInt32
+path count. Each path has a byte layer tag (1 coastline, 2 lake, 3 river), a
+little-endian UInt32 vertex count, and little-endian Int32 latitude and longitude
+pairs. The decoder rejects malformed or excessive geometry.
+
+`Project.siteCoordinate` is nil for older workspaces. Its wire format contains
+`latitudeE7` and `longitudeE7` when a pin exists. Capture the visible project ID,
+its expected pin, and any needed caller navigation/session authority before an
+interaction. Use the committed repository snapshot and transact at the captured
+revision for save and clear.
+
+```swift
+try await repository.transact(expectedRevision: revision) {
+  try $0.setSiteCoordinate(projectID: projectID, expected: priorPin, to: nextPin)
+}
+```
+
+Pass nil as `nextPin` to clear. The workspace checks the project exists, matches
+the effective selection (explicit selection or first project), and still has the
+expected prior pin. The transaction owns validation, revision advancement, and
+atomic persistence. This edit is local, with the existing drafts and outbox
+preserved. Callers can skip no-op writes after confirming the committed state.
+
+`SiteMapFix(coordinate:accuracyMeters:)` is a transient value for the active
+foreground request. Keep it in the map owner and discard it when the request
+or screen ends. Unknown accuracy is nil. Coordinates and known accuracy require
+valid finite bounds. Explicit user action supplies `nextPin` independently of
+projecting a fix.
+
+Call `SiteMapScene.project(site:fix:widthMeters:geography:)` with a width between
+20,000 and 1,000,000 meters. The default is 200,000 meters. It returns nil when
+both anchors are absent, otherwise centering on the site or, with no site, the
+foreground fix. The fix marker is omitted when outside the viewport. Render the
+square viewport with x rightward and y downward, clipped to 0–1. Draw the scale
+bar using `scale.fractionOfWidth` and format `scale.meters` for the locale.
+`fix.accuracyRadius` is relative to viewport width. Clip the accuracy circle when
+drawing. At either pole, the center longitude sets the orientation.
+
+Run `Tests/SiteMapHost/run.sh` on macOS for the model and scene replay. It builds
+each source copy with its existing storage target and compares their readbacks.
